## What Problem This Solves

Three module-level `Set<string>` warning dedupe caches grow unbounded with per-path/per-message keys:

| Cache | File | Key space |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `safeBinTrustedDirWarningCache` | `invoke-system-run.ts` | warning message text per trusted-dir mismatch |
| `chmodWarnedTargets` | `openclaw-state-db.ts` | file path per failed chmod |
| `clobberCapWarnedPaths` | `io.clobber-snapshot.ts` | config path per clobber snapshot overflow |

All three use `.has()` → `.add()`, no eviction, no size cap. Matches the pattern fixed in #101696 and #101738.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace `new Set<string>()` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` from `src/infra/dedupe.js`. The `.check()` method replaces both `.has()` and `.add()` in a single LRU-aware call.

## User Impact

No change for processes operating below 4096 distinct warning keys per cache. Processes exceeding the cap may see one extra warning per evicted entry — a bounded trade-off versus prior unbounded memory growth.

## Real behavior proof

**Real environment tested:** Linux x64 (kernel 4.19.112), Node.js v24.13.1, OpenClaw commit at PR head.

**Exact steps or command run after this patch:**

```bash
npx tsx live-proof.ts
```

**`live-proof.ts` source:**

```ts
import { createDedupeCache } from "./src/infra/dedupe.js";

const CACHE_CAP = 4096;

// Proof 1: Eviction past the 4096-entry cap
console.log("=== Proof 1: Eviction past the 4096-entry cap ===\n");

const cache = createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: CACHE_CAP });
for (let i = 1; i <= CACHE_CAP; i++) {
  const isDuplicate = cache.check(`warning-key-${i}`);
  if (isDuplicate) {
    console.log(`UNEXPECTED duplicate at key-${i} during fill`);
    process.exit(1);
  }
}
console.log("→ Filled cache with", cache.size(), "distinct keys.");
console.log("→ No duplicates during fill (expected).");

const pushed = cache.check(`warning-key-${CACHE_CAP + 1}`);
console.log("→ key-", CACHE_CAP + 1, " pushed past cap: duplicate=", pushed, " (expected: false)");
console.log("→ Cache size after overflow:", cache.size());

const recheck = cache.check("warning-key-1");
console.log("→ Re-check warning-key-1 after eviction: duplicate=", recheck, " (expected: false — evicted)");

if (recheck) {
  console.log("FAIL: oldest key was not evicted past the 4096 cap");
  process.exit(1);
}

// Proof 2: Hot-key LRU retention (touch-on-read)
console.log("\n=== Proof 2: Hot-key LRU retention (touch-on-read) ===\n");

const hotCache = createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 16 });
for (let i = 1; i <= 15; i++) hotCache.check(`entry-${i}`);
for (let i = 0; i < 42; i++) hotCache.check("hot-entry");
console.log("→ Touched \"hot-entry\" 42 times. Cache size:", hotCache.size());

hotCache.check("extra-1");
hotCache.check("extra-2");
console.log("→ Pushed 2 extra entries past cap. Cache size:", hotCache.size());

console.log("→ Re-check \"hot-entry\": duplicate=", hotCache.check("hot-entry"), " (expected: true — retained by LRU)");
console.log("→ Re-check \"entry-1\" (oldest): duplicate=", hotCache.check("entry-1"), " (expected: false — evicted)");

const survived = hotCache.check("hot-entry");
if (!survived) {
  console.log("FAIL: hot key was evicted despite frequent touch-on-read");
  process.exit(1);
}

console.log("\n=== Summary ===");
console.log("createDedupeCache (ttlMs=0, maxSize=4096) — the production primitive used by all 3 caches:");
console.log("  1. Cache stays at 4096 entries maximum.");
console.log("  2. Oldest untouched entries are evicted on overflow.");
console.log("  3. Frequently accessed entries survive via LRU touch-on-read.");
console.log("  4. safeBinTrustedDirWarningCache, chmodWarnedTargets, and");
console.log("     clobberCapWarnedPaths all use this same bounded primitive");
console.log("     — only the key space differs per cache.");
console.log("\nPASS: bounded cache behavior verified.\n");
```

**After-fix evidence:**

```
=== Proof 1: Eviction past the 4096-entry cap ===

→ Filled cache with 4096 distinct keys.
→ No duplicates during fill (expected).
→ key- 4097  pushed past cap: duplicate= false  (expected: false)
→ Cache size after overflow: 4096
→ Re-check warning-key-1 after eviction: duplicate= false  (expected: false — evicted)

=== Proof 2: Hot-key LRU retention (touch-on-read) ===

→ Touched "hot-entry" 42 times. Cache size: 16
→ Pushed 2 extra entries past cap. Cache size: 16
→ Re-check "hot-entry": duplicate= true  (expected: true — retained by LRU)
→ Re-check "entry-1" (oldest): duplicate= false  (expected: false — evicted)

=== Summary ===
createDedupeCache (ttlMs=0, maxSize=4096) — the production primitive used by all 3 caches:
  1. Cache stays at 4096 entries maximum.
  2. Oldest untouched entries are evicted on overflow.
  3. Frequently accessed entries survive via LRU touch-on-read.
  4. safeBinTrustedDirWarningCache, chmodWarnedTargets, and
     clobberCapWarnedPaths all use this same bounded primitive
     — only the key space differs per cache.

PASS: bounded cache behavior verified.
```

**Observed result after fix:** The production primitive (`createDedupeCache`) correctly caps at 4096 entries and evicts the oldest untouched entry on overflow. Hot keys survive eviction via LRU touch-on-read. All three caches in this PR (`safeBinTrustedDirWarningCache`, `chmodWarnedTargets`, `clobberCapWarnedPaths`) are backed by this same primitive — the fix replaces `new Set<string>()` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`, which is the exact code path exercised above.

**Regression test:** All affected test suites pass:

```
pnpm test -- src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts     → 34 passed
pnpm test -- src/state/openclaw-state-db.test.ts         → 21 passed
pnpm test -- src/config/io.clobber-snapshot.test.ts      →  7 passed
```

**What was not tested:** End-to-end 4096-entry eviction through `ensureOpenClawStatePermissions` or `warnWritableTrustedDirOnce` (both require filesystem/environment conditions not reproducible in CI — the bounded-cache primitive already has full coverage).

AI-assisted.

